cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhotoDeg-Bench, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "PhotoDeg-Bench: an open, harmonized benchmark of visible-light polymer deconstruction conditions and outcomes"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
authors:
  - family-names: "Cobbold"
    given-names: "Boris Ekonde"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Knoxville, TN, USA"
    email: "boris.cobbold@yahoo.com"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/boriscobbold-hub/photodeg-bench"
abstract: >-
  Source-verified records of visible-light photochemical polymer deconstruction
  experiments from the open-access literature: polymer, molar mass before and after,
  SEC calibration, catalyst, wavelength, solvent, time and product yields, with
  harmonization rules and comparability tiers. Curated by an AI system under the
  author's delegation, with deterministic source verification and independent
  blind re-extraction.
keywords:
  - polymer upcycling
  - photocatalysis
  - visible light
  - depolymerization
  - size-exclusion chromatography
  - benchmark dataset
